# Drop-in TEMPLATE: the signer's RPC allow list.
#
# deploy/install.sh renders this into
#   /etc/systemd/system/kaiba-signer.service.d/10-rpc-allow.conf
# substituting @RPC_ALLOW_LINES@ with one `IPAddressAllow=` line per entry in
# KAIBA_RPC_ALLOW_CIDRS (set in /etc/kaiba/deploy.env, space or comma separated).
#
# Why a template and not a literal: the RPC endpoints are deployment data. Hardcoding a
# provider's address range in the repository makes the unit wrong for anyone else's box
# and stale the moment the provider re-IPs.
#
# How to find the ranges: resolve each RPC hostname you actually configured
# (SOLANA_RPC_URL, ROBINHOOD_RPC_URL, BSC_RPC_URL, BASE_RPC_URL, ETH_RPC_URL) and use the
# provider's published egress ranges where they publish them. Prefer a /32 you verified
# over a wide CIDR you guessed.
#
# Caveat worth knowing before you rely on this: IPAddressAllow is an eBPF cgroup filter
# on addresses, so a provider behind a large CDN range effectively needs that whole
# range allowed. If the list you end up with is broad enough to be meaningless, switch
# the signer to sign-only mode (PrivateNetwork=yes, see the comments in
# kaiba-signer.service) and let the engine do the network work. That is the stronger
# posture and it needs no allow list at all.

[Service]
IPAddressDeny=any
IPAddressAllow=localhost
@RPC_ALLOW_LINES@
